## Source
2026-06-04 foundations audit: Postel's law (spec + PEP section 11)
promises strict-on-write, but enforcement is scattered per-command;
there is no named universal guard "every write command's output
re-validates clean". Separately, v1HeaderKeys (ergspecv1.go) can grow
without a matching invalid-fixture, silently shrinking validation
coverage. Note: tests/test_datasafety.sh lossless tests already cover
body-preservation and log-append per command -- reference, do not
duplicate.

## Fix
1. Round-trip guard: for each mutating command (new, log, close, tag,
   untag, archive, migrate) run against a fixture store, then
   erg validate every touched file and assert PASS. One loop, one
   guard, future commands join automatically via the dispatch
   registry.
2. Closed-set growth meta-test: every key in v1HeaderKeys must have a
   golden invalid fixture (or an entry in an explicit exemption list)
   exercising its validation path.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Round-trip guard covers all mutating commands from the registry
- [ ] Meta-test fails when a header key is added without fixture
- [ ] make check passes
